CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN VICTIMS OF VIOLENCE
Article 18
Women and children victims of violence shall receive the following rights: a. the right to have their dignity and worth as human beings respected; b. the right to recovery;
c. the right to determine their own decisions;
d. the right to obtain information;
e. the right to confidentiality;
f. the right to social rehabilitation;
g. the right to complaint handling that is prompt, appropriate, comfortable and in accordance with their needs;
h. the right of victims and their families to obtain facilitation in the judicial process;
i. the right to assistance; and - 11 -
j. the right to security and protection.

text:
Pasal 19
Anak korban tindak kekerasan selain mendapatkan hak sebagaimana dimaksud  dalam pasal 18, juga mendapatkan hak khusus sebagai berikut:
a. hak untuk kelangsungan hidup, tumbuh dan berkembang;
b. hak pelayanan dasar kependudukan;
c. hak Perlindungan yang sama;
d. hak bebas dari berbagai stigma; dan
e. hak mendapatkan kebebasan.

translated_text:
Article 19
Child victims of acts of violence in addition to obtaining rights as referred to in article 18, also obtain special rights as follows:
a. right to survival, growth and development;
b. right to basic population services;
c. right to equal Protection;
d. right to be free from various stigma; and
e. right to obtain freedom.

