GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 25
(1) Regional Government conducts guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(2) Guidance and supervision as referred to in paragraph (1), includes: a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance and training;
c. coordination;
d. monitoring;
e. evaluation; and
f. reporting.
